# The planning-only path list (AGENTS.md § "The gate").
#
# A pull request whose changed paths are all listed here passes `Full gate` without a build or a
# test. `.github/workflows/classify-change.yml` reads this file from the pull request's base
# commit, so a pull request that changes it is classified by the list it found, under which this
# file is code.
#
# A path is listed when it matches an `include` pattern and no `exclude` pattern. A pattern is
# matched against the whole path from the repository root, `*` matches any run of characters,
# `/` included, and a pattern holds only letters, digits and `. _ / - *`. A line that is neither
# a comment, an `include` nor an `exclude` makes every pull request `code`.
#
# The list names the trees that hold planning and prose. Every other path is code, Markdown
# included: `website/` is the built site, `CHANGELOG.md` is compared with the site's release
# page, `STATUS.md` holds the release lines `cargo xtask check-docs` compares with the workspace
# version (`xtask/src/site_release.rs`), `contracts/` and `xtask/bundle-source/` are released
# bundle bytes and their sources, `README.md`, `AGENTS.md` and the crate READMEs are read by tests
# or compiled as doctests, and `spec/`, `deploy/` and `vendor/` are sources.
include .engineering/*
include adr/*.md
include architecture/*.md
include docs/*.md
include ROADMAP.md
include SECURITY.md
include glossary.md

# Documents in those trees that a test reads by name. A change to one can fail that test, so it
# is code. `xtask/tests/planning_only_classification.rs` fails when Rust source names a listed
# Markdown file that has no line here.
exclude adr/0047-a-kubernetes-namespace-driver-serves-workspaces-on-pvcs-and-execs-as-pods.md
exclude docs/design/04-security-and-isolation.md
exclude docs/design/08-phase-3-closure-invariants.md
